G5613:
ὡς, adverbial form of the relative pron. ὅς, ἥ, ὅ.
I. As relat. adv. of manner, as, like as, just as, even as;
1. with a demonstrative, like οὕτως, expressed or understood: οὕτως . . . ὡς, Mark 4:26, 1 Corinthians 3:15, Ephesians 5:28, James 2:12, al.; ὡς . . . οὕτως, Acts 8:32, 1 Corinthians 7:17, al.; elliptically (sc. οὕτως, οὕτω), c. nom., Matthew 6:29, al.; c. acc., Matthew 19:19, Mark 12:31, al.; c. prep., Matthew 26:55, Mark 14:48, Luke 22:52, John 7:10, al.; c. verb., John 15:6, 2 Corinthians 3:1, Ephesians 2:3, 1 Thessalonians 5:6, al.; c. ptcp. (the ptcp. however not having the special force wh. it has in cl.; v. Bl., §73, 5; 74, 6), Matthew 7:29, Mark 1:22, Hebrews 13:17, al.; freq implying opinion or belief, Romans 9:32; so esp, c. gen. absol., 1 Corinthians 4:18, 2 Corinthians 5:20, 1 Peter 4:12, 2 Peter 1:3.
2. Before numerals, about, nearly: Mark 5:13, John 1:40, Acts 5:7, al.
3. Before adjectives and adverbs, how: Romans 10:15 Romans 11:33, 1 Thessalonians 2:10; c. superl., ὡς τάχιστα, as quickly as possible, Acts 17:15.
II. As conjunction;
1. temporal,
(a) as, when, since: Mark 9:21 Mark 14:72, Luke 1:23, John 2:9, al.;
(b) while, when, as long as: Luke 12:58, John 12:36, Galatians 6:10 (Field, Notes, 191); ὡς ἄν (M, Pr., 167, and v.s. ἄν), Romans 15:24, 1 Corinthians 11:34, Philippians 2:23.
2. Final, in order that; c. inf., in order to (M, Pr., 204n), Luke 9:52, Acts 20:24, Hebrews 7:9.

G5616:
ὡσεί adv.,
(a) as if, .as it were, like as, like: Matthew 3:16 Matthew 9:36, Acts 2:3 Acts 6:15, Romans 6:13, Hebrews 1:12; γίνεσθαι (φαίνεσθαι) ὡσεί, Mark 9:26, Luke 22:44 ([WH] R, mg., om.), Luke 24:11;
(b) in calculation, and with numbers, about: Matthew 14:21, Luke 3:23 Luke 9:14, Luke 9:28 Luke 22:41, Luke 22:59 Luke 23:44, Acts 2:41 Acts 10:3 Acts 19:7; ὡσεὶ λίθου βολήν, Luke 22:41.†
